// The generators' parameter channels, "along" and "around" (extrude, sweep,
// sweepScaled and lathe record each vertex's place in the generator), their
// carry through every later operator, and 'displaceAlongNormal', checked
// with the testing package against values worked out by hand; only a
// failure prints, so channels.out holds the summary alone.
//
// - A sweep of the unit square S = (0,0) (1,0) (1,1) (0,1) along the straight
//   path (0,0,0) to (0,0,1) in 4 equal pieces, with caps: 5 rings of 4, 20
//   vertices; vertex 4i + j is S's point j at path point i. along is s / L
//   = i / 4: 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1. S is 4 long and each side 1, so around
//   is j / 4: 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75. Both are f32 vertex channels, 20 values
//   each, beside the corner "uv" (one Vec2 channel, two float channels).
//   The seam: S closes from point 3 back to point 0, so face 3 (the closing
//   band's first quad, (0, 3), (0, 0), (1, 0), (1, 3)) has corner 1 at
//   vertex 0 with uv u = 1, while vertex 0's around is 0. The caps make no
//   vertices: the start cap, face 16, is 3, 2, 1, 0, all along 0; the end
//   cap, face 17, is 16 to 19, all along 1.
// - Along an uneven path, (0,0,0) (0,0,1) (0,0,4): 1 and 3 long, L = 4, so
//   along is 0, 0.25, 1 by distance, not 0, 0.5, 1 by point.
// - The square extruded along (0,0,2) in 2 segments: along i / 2 = 0, 0.5,
//   1; and along (0,0,-2), its faces turned over, the same along (by ring,
//   not by direction).
// - A torus, the diamond of radius 0.5 swept round Path.circle(2, 4): 4
//   equal chords, so along is k / 4 for ring k, ring 0 (the seam) 0 and
//   ring 3 0.75; face 15, vertices 15, 12, 0, 3, has uv (1, 1) at vertex 0,
//   whose along and around are both 0.
// - sweepScaled (here a scale of 1) writes them too: along 16 pieces, ring 1
//   is along 1/16 = 0.0625.
// - A lathe of the segment (1, 0) to (1, 2) about +y, a whole turn in 4
//   steps: vertex 4j + k is profile point j in column k. along is the
//   angle's fraction k / 4: vertex 1 0.25, vertex 7 0.75, vertex 4 0;
//   around is the profile's fraction, 0 for vertices 0-3 and 1 for 4-7.
//   Face 3, 3, 0, 4, 7, closes the turn: its corner 1 (vertex 0) has u = 1
//   in "uv", and vertex 0 has along 0. A half turn in 2 steps is open, 3
//   columns: vertex 2 has along 1 (no seam). The profile (1, 0) (1, 1)
//   (1, 3), 1 and 2 long, gives around 0, 1/3, 1 (vertices 0, 4, 8). The
//   octahedron, (0, -1) (1, 0) (0, 1) lathed: vertex 0 (the bottom pole)
//   has along 0 and around 0; vertices 1 to 4, the middle point's columns,
//   along 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, around 0.5 (two pieces of equal length); vertex
//   5, the top pole, along 0, around 1.
// - The carry chain: the square swept along (0,0,0) to (0,0,1) in 4 pieces,
//   no caps (an open tube: 20 vertices, 36 edges, 16 quads), then bent a
//   quarter turn about +y along +z from the origin: R = 1 / (pi/2) and the
//   bend turns +z towards +x, so vertex 16 at (0, 0, 1) goes to (R, 0, R) =
//   (0.636620, 0, 0.636620), its along still 1. Then subdivided once: V + E +
//   F = 20 + 36 + 16 = 72 vertices; vertex v keeps its number, edge e's
//   point is 20 + e, face f's 56 + f. along is i / 4, a linear function of
//   the ring, and Catmull-Clark reproduces it on this grid: an interior
//   vertex of valence 4 at ring i has face points averaging (2 a_i + a_{i-1}
//   + a_{i+1}) / 4 = a_i and edge midpoints averaging a_i, so (F + 2R + P) /
//   4 = a_i; a boundary vertex (ring 0 or 4) follows its boundary
//   neighbours, all on its ring. So vertex 8 stays 0.5, 0 stays 0 and 16
//   stays 1; the edge from vertex 4 to vertex 8 (rings 1 and 2) gets (a + b
//   + 2 (a + b) / 2) / 4 = 0.375; the ring edge 8-9 gets 0.5; face 12 (rings
//   3 and 4) gets its corners' mean, (0.75 + 0.75 + 1 + 1) / 4 = 0.875.
//   around shows the seam: away from it, vertex 9 (around 0.25, neighbours
//   0 and 0.5 in its ring) stays 0.25 and vertex 10 stays 0.5; but vertex 8,
//   the seam (around 0, its ring neighbours 0.25 and 0.75), gets face points
//   0.125, 0.125, 0.375, 0.375 (F = 0.25) and edge midpoints 0.125, 0.375,
//   0, 0 (R = 0.125), so (0.25 + 0.25 + 0) / 4 = 0.125: the vertex rules
//   blend 0 with the 0.75 across the seam. Then a linear array of 2, offset
//   (3, 0, 0): copy 1's vertex v is 72 + v with v's values and v's position
//   moved by (3, 0, 0): vertex 80 along 0.5, 140 along 0.875.
// - Every other operator carries them, on the open tube T:
//   - mirror in x = 5: vertex 20 + v is v's copy, its along v's;
//   - a linear array of 2, offset (0, 0, 1), unmerged, welded at 0.001:
//     copy 1's ring 0 (vertices 20-23) lies on copy 0's ring 4 (16-19) and
//     merges into it, keeping its lowest-numbered vertex's values (along
//     1); 36 vertices left, copy 1's vertex 24 (ring 1) now 20 with along
//     0.25, and 35 (copy 1's last) along 1; the array with its own merge
//     gives the same;
//   - extruding face 5 (vertices 5, 6, 10, 9) by 0.5: new vertices 20 to 23
//     are 5's, 6's, 10's and 9's copies, along 0.25, 0.25, 0.5, 0.5 and
//     around 0.25, 0.5, 0.5, 0.25; insetting face 5 by 0.1 the same;
//   - solidify 0.1 with a rim: vertex 20 + v is v's copy, so 28 has along
//     0.5;
//   - smoothing, the lattice, twist, taper and curveDeform move vertices
//     only: both channels come back bit for bit.
// - displaceAlongNormal on a cylinder: the open profile (1, 0) (1, 0.5)
//   (1, 1) (1, 1.5) (1, 2) lathed a whole turn about +y in 4 steps; vertex
//   4j + k is point j in column k, column k at k quarter turns (x to -z), so
//   (1, y) goes to (1, y, 0), (0, y, -1), (-1, y, 0), (0, y, 1). Every
//   vertex's faces are rectangles meeting it at 90 degrees, two of them
//   either side of the radius, so its normal is the radius, outward. around
//   is j / 4. By "around" and 0.5, point j moves out by 0.5 j / 4: vertex 0
//   stays at (1, 0, 0), vertex 10 (j = 2, column 2) goes to (-1.25, 1, 0),
//   vertex 17 (j = 4, column 1) to (0, 2, -1.5). Ribs from a channel the
//   caller filled, "rib" 1 on profile points 1 and 3 and 0 elsewhere, and
//   0.25: vertex 4 (1, 0.5, 0) goes to (1.25, 0.5, 0), vertex 13 (j = 3,
//   column 1) to (0, 1.5, -1.25), vertex 8 stays (1, 1, 0). Face 0 is 0, 1,
//   5, 4: (1, 0, 0), (0, 0, -1), (0, 0.5, -1.25), (1.25, 0.5, 0), a
//   trapezoid; (B - A) x (C - A) = (-1, 0, -1) x (-1, 0.5, -1.25) = (0.5,
//   -0.25, -0.5), length 0.75, so its normal is (0.666667, -0.333333,
//   -0.666667): still outward, tilted down as the rib flares. An empty
//   name, or a channel the mesh lacks, moves every vertex by the amount:
//   vertex 6 (j = 1, column 2) by 0.25 to (-1.25, 0.5, 0). Topology and
//   channels are unchanged.

mod channels;

import testing use *;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import mesh use *;
import sculpt use *;

imm near = 0.00001d;

fn point(got Vec3, x f32, y f32, z f32, label &Array[u8]) {
  expectFloat(got.x, x, near, label);
  expectFloat(got.y, y, near, label);
  expectFloat(got.z, z, near, label);
}

// The value of a vertex channel named 'name' at vertex v
fn value(m &PolyMesh, name &str, v u32) f32 {
  imm ch = m.findFloatChannel(VertexDomain, name);
  if ch == NoIndex { return -1.; }
  m.float(ch, v);
}

fn along(m &PolyMesh, v u32, want f32, label &Array[u8]) {expectFloat(value(m, "along", v), want, near, label);}
fn around(m &PolyMesh, v u32, want f32, label &Array[u8]) {expectFloat(value(m, "around", v), want, near, label);}

// 'validate' clean
fn clean(m &PolyMesh, label &Array[u8]) {
  imm problems = m.validate();
  if !expectInt(i64.from(problems.len()), 0, label) {
    mut i = 0usize;
    while i < problems.len() {
      expectStr(problems[i].view(), "", label);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
  }
}

// Both channels there, as vertex channels with a value per vertex
fn hasChannels(m &PolyMesh, label &Array[u8]) {
  imm a = m.findFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "along");
  imm r = m.findFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "around");
  if !expectBool(a != NoIndex and r != NoIndex, true, label) { return; }
  expectInt(i64.from(m.floats[usize.from(a)].values.len()), i64.from(m.vertexCount()), label);
  expectInt(i64.from(m.floats[usize.from(r)].values.len()), i64.from(m.vertexCount()), label);
}

// Both channels the same, bit for bit, in two meshes of the same vertices
fn sameChannels(a &PolyMesh, b &PolyMesh, label &Array[u8]) {
  if !expectInt(i64.from(b.vertexCount()), i64.from(a.vertexCount()), label) { return; }
  mut diff = 0i64;
  mut v = 0u32;
  while usize.from(v) < a.vertexCount() {
    if value(a, "along", v) != value(b, "along", v) { diff = diff + 1; }
    if value(a, "around", v) != value(b, "around", v) { diff = diff + 1; }
    v = v + 1u32;
  }
  expectInt(diff, 0, label);
}

// The uv of a face's corner k
fn cornerUv(m &PolyMesh, f u32, k usize) Vec2 {
  imm ch = m.findVec2Channel(CornerDomain, "uv");
  imm hs = m.faceHalfedges(f);
  m.vec2(ch, *hs[k]);
}

// The edge joining vertices a and b, or NoIndex
fn edgeBetween(m &PolyMesh, a u32, b u32) u32 {
  imm hs = m.vertexOutgoing(a);
  mut i = 0usize;
  while i < hs.len() {
    if m.toVertex(*hs[i]) == b { return m.edge(*hs[i]); }
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  NoIndex;
}

fn unitSquare() Profile {
  imm sq Array[Vec2, 4] = [new Vec2(0., 0.), new Vec2(1., 0.), new Vec2(1., 1.), new Vec2(0., 1.)];
  Profile.fromPoints(&sq, true);
}

// The square swept along z from 0 to 1 in 4 pieces, open at both ends
fn openTube() PolyMesh {
  imm s = unitSquare();
  imm path = Path.line(new Vec3(0., 0., 0.), new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), 4u32);
  sweep(&s, &path, 0., 1., 1., false);
}

fn unitScale(u f32) f32 { 1.; }

fn sweeps() {
  imm s = unitSquare();
  imm path = Path.line(new Vec3(0., 0., 0.), new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), 4u32);
  imm m = sweep(&s, &path, 0., 1., 1., true);
  clean(&m, "sweep: validates");
  requireInt(i64.from(m.vertexCount()), 20, "sweep: 20 vertices");
  hasChannels(&m, "sweep: along and around");
  expectInt(i64.from(m.floats.len()), 2, "sweep: two float channels");
  expectInt(i64.from(m.vec2s.len()), 1, "sweep: one Vec2 channel, uv");
  mut i = 0u32;
  while i < 5u32 {
    mut j = 0u32;
    while j < 4u32 {
      along(&m, 4u32 * i + j, f32.from(i) * 0.25, "sweep: along is i / 4");
      around(&m, 4u32 * i + j, f32.from(j) * 0.25, "sweep: around is j / 4");
      j = j + 1u32;
    }
    i = i + 1u32;
  }
  along(&m, 8u32, 0.5, "sweep: vertex 8 halfway");
  around(&m, 0u32, 0., "sweep: the seam vertex has around 0");
  imm f3 = m.faceVertices(3u32);
  expectInt(i64.from(*f3[1usize]), 0, "sweep: face 3's corner 1 is vertex 0");
  expectFloat(cornerUv(&m, 3u32, 1usize).x, 1., near, "sweep: where its corner uv has u = 1");
  imm startCap = m.faceVertices(16u32);
  imm endCap = m.faceVertices(17u32);
  requireInt(i64.from(startCap.len()), 4, "sweep: start cap");
  requireInt(i64.from(endCap.len()), 4, "sweep: end cap");
  i = 0u32;
  while i < 4u32 {
    along(&m, *startCap[usize.from(i)], 0., "sweep: start cap vertices along 0");
    along(&m, *endCap[usize.from(i)], 1., "sweep: end cap vertices along 1");
    i = i + 1u32;
  }

  imm uneven Array[Vec3, 3] = [new Vec3(0., 0., 0.), new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), new Vec3(0., 0., 4.)];
  imm up = Path.fromPoints(&uneven, false);
  imm u = sweep(&s, &up, 0., 1., 1., false);
  along(&u, 0u32, 0., "uneven path: along 0");
  along(&u, 4u32, 0.25, "uneven path: along 1 / 4, by distance");
  along(&u, 9u32, 1., "uneven path: along 1");

  imm e = extrude(&s, new Vec3(0., 0., 2.), 2u32, true);
  hasChannels(&e, "extrude: along and around");
  along(&e, 0u32, 0., "extrude: ring 0");
  along(&e, 5u32, 0.5, "extrude: ring 1");
  along(&e, 11u32, 1., "extrude: ring 2");
  around(&e, 6u32, 0.5, "extrude: point 2");
  imm down = extrude(&s, new Vec3(0., 0., -2.), 2u32, true);
  along(&down, 5u32, 0.5, "extrude down: along by ring");
  along(&down, 11u32, 1., "extrude down: along by ring");
  around(&down, 7u32, 0.75, "extrude down: around by profile");

  imm d = Profile.polygon(4u32, 0.5);
  imm ring = Path.circle(2., 4u32);
  imm t = sweep(&d, &ring, 0., 1., 1., true);
  hasChannels(&t, "torus: along and around");
  along(&t, 0u32, 0., "torus: ring 0, the seam, along 0");
  along(&t, 5u32, 0.25, "torus: ring 1");
  along(&t, 14u32, 0.75, "torus: ring 3");
  around(&t, 14u32, 0.5, "torus: point 2");
  imm tv = t.faceVertices(15u32);
  expectInt(i64.from(*tv[2usize]), 0, "torus: face 15's corner 2 is vertex 0");
  expectFloat(cornerUv(&t, 15u32, 2usize).x, 1., near, "torus: its uv u is 1");
  expectFloat(cornerUv(&t, 15u32, 2usize).y, 1., near, "torus: its uv v is 1");
  around(&t, 0u32, 0., "torus: vertex 0 around 0");

  imm dia = Profile.polygon(4u32, 1.);
  imm zpath = Path.line(new Vec3(0., 0., 0.), new Vec3(0., 0., 2.), 16u32);
  imm r = sweepScaled(&dia, &zpath, 0., true, u => 1.);
  hasChannels(&r, "sweepScaled: along and around");
  along(&r, 4u32, 0.0625, "sweepScaled: ring 1 along 1 / 16");
  along(&r, 67u32, 1., "sweepScaled: the last ring along 1");
}

fn lathes() {
  imm seg Array[Vec2, 2] = [new Vec2(1., 0.), new Vec2(1., 2.)];
  imm s = Profile.fromPoints(&seg, false);
  imm c = lathe(&s, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), 2. * pi, 4u32);
  requireInt(i64.from(c.vertexCount()), 8, "lathe: 8 vertices");
  hasChannels(&c, "lathe: along and around");
  along(&c, 0u32, 0., "lathe: column 0, the seam");
  along(&c, 1u32, 0.25, "lathe: column 1");
  along(&c, 7u32, 0.75, "lathe: column 3");
  along(&c, 4u32, 0., "lathe: column 0 at the top");
  around(&c, 2u32, 0., "lathe: the bottom point");
  around(&c, 6u32, 1., "lathe: the top point");
  imm f3 = c.faceVertices(3u32);
  expectInt(i64.from(*f3[1usize]), 0, "lathe: face 3's corner 1 is vertex 0");
  expectFloat(cornerUv(&c, 3u32, 1usize).x, 1., near, "lathe: where its corner uv has u = 1");

  imm half = lathe(&s, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), pi, 2u32);
  along(&half, 1u32, 0.5, "half turn: column 1");
  along(&half, 2u32, 1., "half turn: column 2, open, along 1");

  imm bent Array[Vec2, 3] = [new Vec2(1., 0.), new Vec2(1., 1.), new Vec2(1., 3.)];
  imm b = Profile.fromPoints(&bent, false);
  imm l = lathe(&b, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), 2. * pi, 4u32);
  around(&l, 0u32, 0., "lathe by length: point 0");
  around(&l, 4u32, 0.333333, "lathe by length: point 1, 1 of 3");
  around(&l, 8u32, 1., "lathe by length: point 2");

  imm arc Array[Vec2, 3] = [new Vec2(0., -1.), new Vec2(1., 0.), new Vec2(0., 1.)];
  imm a = Profile.fromPoints(&arc, false);
  imm o = lathe(&a, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), 2. * pi, 4u32);
  requireInt(i64.from(o.vertexCount()), 6, "octahedron: 6 vertices");
  hasChannels(&o, "octahedron: along and around");
  along(&o, 0u32, 0., "octahedron: the bottom pole, along 0");
  around(&o, 0u32, 0., "octahedron: the bottom pole, around 0");
  along(&o, 1u32, 0., "octahedron: column 0");
  along(&o, 2u32, 0.25, "octahedron: column 1");
  along(&o, 3u32, 0.5, "octahedron: column 2");
  along(&o, 4u32, 0.75, "octahedron: column 3");
  around(&o, 3u32, 0.5, "octahedron: the middle point");
  along(&o, 5u32, 0., "octahedron: the top pole, along 0");
  around(&o, 5u32, 1., "octahedron: the top pole, around 1");
}

fn chain() {
  imm t = openTube();
  requireInt(i64.from(t.vertexCount()), 20, "chain: 20 vertices");
  requireInt(i64.from(t.edgeCount()), 36, "chain: 36 edges");
  requireInt(i64.from(t.faceCount()), 16, "chain: 16 faces");
  imm b = bend(&t, pi / 2., new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), new Vec3(0., 0., 0.));
  point(*b.positions[16usize], 0.636620, 0., 0.636620, "chain: the bend moved vertex 16");
  along(&b, 16u32, 1., "chain: after the bend, vertex 16 along 1");
  along(&b, 8u32, 0.5, "chain: after the bend, vertex 8 along 0.5");

  imm s = subdivide(&b, 1u32);
  clean(&s, "chain: subdivided validates");
  requireInt(i64.from(s.vertexCount()), 72, "chain: 72 vertices");
  hasChannels(&s, "chain: subdivided keeps along and around");
  along(&s, 0u32, 0., "chain: vertex 0 stays 0");
  along(&s, 8u32, 0.5, "chain: vertex 8 stays 0.5");
  along(&s, 16u32, 1., "chain: vertex 16 stays 1");
  imm e48 = edgeBetween(&t, 4u32, 8u32);
  requireBool(e48 != NoIndex, true, "chain: edge 4-8");
  along(&s, 20u32 + e48, 0.375, "chain: edge 4-8's point, between rings 1 and 2");
  imm e89 = edgeBetween(&t, 8u32, 9u32);
  requireBool(e89 != NoIndex, true, "chain: edge 8-9");
  along(&s, 20u32 + e89, 0.5, "chain: edge 8-9's point, on ring 2");
  imm e01 = edgeBetween(&t, 0u32, 1u32);
  along(&s, 20u32 + e01, 0., "chain: boundary edge 0-1's point");
  imm e1617 = edgeBetween(&t, 16u32, 17u32);
  along(&s, 20u32 + e1617, 1., "chain: boundary edge 16-17's point");
  along(&s, 56u32 + 12u32, 0.875, "chain: face 12's point, between rings 3 and 4");
  around(&s, 9u32, 0.25, "chain: vertex 9's around, away from the seam");
  around(&s, 10u32, 0.5, "chain: vertex 10's around, away from the seam");
  around(&s, 8u32, 0.125, "chain: vertex 8's around, the seam blended");

  imm arr = arrayLinear(&s, 2u32, new Vec3(3., 0., 0.), -1.);
  requireInt(i64.from(arr.vertexCount()), 144, "chain: the array's 144 vertices");
  hasChannels(&arr, "chain: the array keeps along and around");
  along(&arr, 8u32, 0.5, "chain: copy 0's vertex 8");
  along(&arr, 80u32, 0.5, "chain: copy 1's vertex 8");
  along(&arr, 140u32, 0.875, "chain: copy 1's face 12 point");
  around(&arr, 80u32, 0.125, "chain: copy 1's vertex 8's around");
  imm p8 = *s.positions[8usize];
  point(*arr.positions[80usize], p8.x + 3., p8.y, p8.z, "chain: copy 1's vertex 8 moved by the offset");
}

fn carried() {
  imm t = openTube();

  imm mi = mirror(&t, new Vec3(5., 0., 0.), new Vec3(1., 0., 0.), -1.);
  requireInt(i64.from(mi.vertexCount()), 40, "mirror: 40 vertices");
  hasChannels(&mi, "mirror: along and around");
  along(&mi, 28u32, 0.5, "mirror: vertex 8's copy");
  around(&mi, 29u32, 0.25, "mirror: vertex 9's copy");

  imm stacked = arrayLinear(&t, 2u32, new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), -1.);
  imm w = weld(&stacked, 0.001);
  requireInt(i64.from(w.vertexCount()), 36, "weld: 36 vertices");
  hasChannels(&w, "weld: along and around");
  along(&w, 16u32, 1., "weld: the merged ring keeps copy 0's along");
  along(&w, 20u32, 0.25, "weld: copy 1's ring 1, renumbered");
  along(&w, 35u32, 1., "weld: copy 1's last vertex");
  around(&w, 21u32, 0.25, "weld: copy 1's ring 1, point 1");
  imm am = arrayLinear(&t, 2u32, new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), 0.001);
  requireInt(i64.from(am.vertexCount()), 36, "array merged: 36 vertices");
  sameChannels(&w, &am, "array merged: as welded");

  imm f5 Array[u32, 1] = [5u32];
  imm ex = extrudeFaces(&t, &f5, 0.5);
  clean(&ex, "extrude face: validates");
  requireInt(i64.from(ex.vertexCount()), 24, "extrude face: 24 vertices");
  hasChannels(&ex, "extrude face: along and around");
  along(&ex, 20u32, 0.25, "extrude face: 5's copy");
  along(&ex, 21u32, 0.25, "extrude face: 6's copy");
  along(&ex, 22u32, 0.5, "extrude face: 10's copy");
  along(&ex, 23u32, 0.5, "extrude face: 9's copy");
  around(&ex, 20u32, 0.25, "extrude face: 5's copy");
  around(&ex, 21u32, 0.5, "extrude face: 6's copy");
  around(&ex, 22u32, 0.5, "extrude face: 10's copy");
  around(&ex, 23u32, 0.25, "extrude face: 9's copy");

  imm ins = inset(&t, &f5, 0.1, 0.);
  requireInt(i64.from(ins.vertexCount()), 24, "inset: 24 vertices");
  hasChannels(&ins, "inset: along and around");
  along(&ins, 20u32, 0.25, "inset: 5's copy");
  along(&ins, 22u32, 0.5, "inset: 10's copy");
  around(&ins, 21u32, 0.5, "inset: 6's copy");

  imm so = solidify(&t, 0.1, 0., false, true);
  requireInt(i64.from(so.vertexCount()), 40, "solidify: 40 vertices");
  hasChannels(&so, "solidify: along and around");
  along(&so, 28u32, 0.5, "solidify: vertex 8's copy");
  around(&so, 39u32, 0.75, "solidify: vertex 19's copy");

  imm sm = smooth(&t, 0.5, 2u32);
  sameChannels(&t, &sm, "smooth: unchanged");
  imm tb = smoothTaubin(&t, 0.5, taubinMu(0.5, TaubinPassBand), 2u32);
  sameChannels(&t, &tb, "Taubin: unchanged");
  mut lat = Lattice.regular(new Vec3(-1., -1., -1.), new Vec3(3., 0., 0.), new Vec3(0., 3., 0.), new Vec3(0., 0., 3.),
    2u32, 2u32, 2u32);
  lat.movePoint(1u32, 1u32, 1u32, new Vec3(0.5, 0.5, 0.5));
  imm la = latticeDeform(&t, &lat, LatticeLinear);
  sameChannels(&t, &la, "lattice: unchanged");
  imm tw = twist(&t, pi / 2., new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), new Vec3(0., 0., 0.));
  sameChannels(&t, &tw, "twist: unchanged");
  imm tp = taper(&t, 1., new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), new Vec3(0., 0., 0.));
  sameChannels(&t, &tp, "taper: unchanged");
  imm circ = Path.circle(2., 16u32);
  imm cd = curveDeform(&t, &circ, new Vec3(0., 0., 1.), new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), new Vec3(0., 0., 0.));
  sameChannels(&t, &cd, "curveDeform: unchanged");
}

fn displacements() {
  imm col Array[Vec2, 5] = [new Vec2(1., 0.), new Vec2(1., 0.5), new Vec2(1., 1.), new Vec2(1., 1.5), new Vec2(1., 2.)];
  imm p = Profile.fromPoints(&col, false);
  imm c = lathe(&p, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), 2. * pi, 4u32);
  requireInt(i64.from(c.vertexCount()), 20, "cylinder: 20 vertices");
  point(*c.positions[17usize], 0., 2., -1., "cylinder: vertex 17");

  imm flare = displaceAlongNormal(&c, "around", 0.5);
  clean(&flare, "by around: validates");
  point(*flare.positions[0usize], 1., 0., 0., "by around: vertex 0 stays");
  point(*flare.positions[10usize], -1.25, 1., 0., "by around: vertex 10 out by 0.25");
  point(*flare.positions[17usize], 0., 2., -1.5, "by around: vertex 17 out by 0.5");

  mut ribbed = displaceAlongNormal(&c, "", 0.);
  imm rib = ribbed.addFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "rib", 0.);
  mut k = 0u32;
  while k < 4u32 {
    ribbed.setFloat(rib, 4u32 + k, 1.);
    ribbed.setFloat(rib, 12u32 + k, 1.);
    k = k + 1u32;
  }
  imm r = displaceAlongNormal(&ribbed, "rib", 0.25);
  clean(&r, "ribs: validates");
  point(*r.positions[4usize], 1.25, 0.5, 0., "ribs: vertex 4 out by 0.25");
  point(*r.positions[13usize], 0., 1.5, -1.25, "ribs: vertex 13 out by 0.25");
  point(*r.positions[8usize], 1., 1., 0., "ribs: vertex 8 stays");
  point(r.faceNormal(0u32), 0.666667, -0.333333, -0.666667, "ribs: face 0 still faces out, tilted");
  expectInt(i64.from(r.faceCount()), i64.from(c.faceCount()), "ribs: the same faces");
  expectInt(i64.from(r.edgeCount()), i64.from(c.edgeCount()), "ribs: the same edges");
  expectInt(i64.from(r.floats.len()), 3, "ribs: along, around and rib carried");
  expectInt(i64.from(r.vec2s.len()), 1, "ribs: uv carried");
  sameChannels(&c, &r, "ribs: along and around unchanged");
  expectFloat(value(&r, "rib", 13u32), 1., near, "ribs: rib unchanged");

  imm all = displaceAlongNormal(&c, "", 0.25);
  point(*all.positions[6usize], -1.25, 0.5, 0., "no channel: every vertex by the amount");
  imm missing = displaceAlongNormal(&c, "nope", 0.25);
  point(*missing.positions[6usize], -1.25, 0.5, 0., "a missing channel: every vertex by the amount");
}

fn main() i32 {
  sweeps();
  lathes();
  chain();
  carried();
  displacements();
  done();
}
